the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base termlife_premium_payment includes these resources:
    temporal.

the functions are:
    the effective date of *an activity* is *a date*.
    the amount of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the modal premium of the policy before *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the paid to date of the policy before *an activity* is *a date*.
    the billing mode of the policy before *an activity* is *a value*.
    the ratio of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the modes paid of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the months per mode of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the months advanced of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the new paid to date of *an activity* is *a date*.
    the unapplied amount of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the paid to date of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.

the templates are:
    *an activity* is a premium payment.
    *an activity* fails the check *a code*.

the knowledge base termlife_premium_payment includes:

the text of "PremiumPayment/Transaction.xml" is at "sources/PremiumPayment/Transaction.xml".

% An activity of this program is a premium payment: the PremiumPayment transaction it processes.
an activity is a premium payment if
    the effective date of the activity is a date.

rule ratio with provenance "PremiumPayment/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable RatioMV:
the ratio of an activity is a number N if
    the amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the modal premium of the policy before the activity is an amount K
    and N = M / K.

rule modes_paid with provenance "PremiumPayment/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable ModesPaidMV:
the modes paid of an activity is an amount N if
    the ratio of the activity is a number M
    and N = truncate(M).

rule months_per_mode with provenance "PremiumPayment/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable MonthsPerModeMV:
the months per mode of an activity is a number N if
    the billing mode of the policy before the activity is a value
    and the value is equal to "12"
    and N = 1
    otherwise the billing mode of the policy before the activity is a second value
    and the second value is equal to "04"
    and N = 3
    otherwise the billing mode of the policy before the activity is a third value
    and the third value is equal to "02"
    and N = 6
    otherwise the activity is a premium payment
    and N = 12.

rule months_advanced with provenance "PremiumPayment/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable MonthsAdvancedMV:
the months advanced of an activity is a number N if
    the modes paid of the activity is an amount M
    and the months per mode of the activity is a number K
    and N = M * K.

rule new_paid_to_date with provenance "PremiumPayment/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable NewPaidToDateMV:
the new paid to date of an activity is a date if
    the date is the months advanced of the activity months after the paid to date of the policy before the activity.

rule unapplied_amount with provenance "PremiumPayment/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable UnappliedAmountMV:
the unapplied amount of an activity is an amount N if
    the amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the modes paid of the activity is an amount K
    and the modal premium of the policy before the activity is an amount P
    and N = round((M - K * P) * 100) / 100.

% A payment of [the amount] is less than one modal premium ([the modal premium]).
rule p001 with provenance "PremiumPayment/ValidateExpressions.xml" at Expression P001:
an activity fails the check "P001" if
    the amount of the activity < the modal premium of the policy before the activity.

rule copy_paid_to_date with provenance "PremiumPayment/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field PaidToDate:
the paid to date of the policy after an activity is a value if
    the new paid to date of the activity is the value
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

scenario monthly_payer_p1 is:
    the effective date of p1 is 2024-04-01.
    the amount of p1 is 100.
    the modal premium of the policy before p1 is 44.189999999999998.
    the paid to date of the policy before p1 is 2024-04-01.
    the billing mode of the policy before p1 is "12".
    new_paid_to_date expects answers ["the new paid to date of p1 is 2024-06-01"].
    unapplied_amount expects answers ["the unapplied amount of p1 is 11.62"].
    checks expects answers [].
    policy_after_paid_to_date expects answers ["the paid to date of the policy after p1 is 2024-06-01"].

